WEBVTT

00:57:57.871 --> 00:58:01.954
do you have a structural advantage in
that your mission is to do this

00:58:01.954 --> 00:58:06.621
for everyone as opposed to for
some corporate objective.

00:58:06.621 --> 00:58:09.329
And that that that allows you that.

00:58:09.454 --> 00:58:12.663
Why is it that we came out of open
eye and not someone else?

00:58:12.704 --> 00:58:16.663
It's like it's surprising in some ways
when you're up against so much money

00:58:16.663 --> 00:58:20.746
and so much talent in these other
companies that you came up with this

00:58:20.746 --> 00:58:21.788
platform ahead of. You know, in

00:58:21.788 --> 00:58:24.038
some sense it's surprising
and in some sense,

00:58:24.038 --> 00:58:25.913
like the startup wins most of the time,

00:58:25.913 --> 00:58:28.913
like I'm a huge believer in
startups as the best force

00:58:28.913 --> 00:58:30.454
for innovation we have in the world today.